{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9tWhkp6ctVAYFUQrMnF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: a path separator in an `--and` pattern now gets the same error the primary pattern already got. Tests pass; nothing is committed.\n\n- **Change in `src/main.rs`:** I moved the separator check into a small helper, `pattern_looks_like_path`. `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now runs it on the primary pattern and on every `--and` pattern, and the error names the first one that fails. The Windows rule (a `\\` pattern is only flagged if it names an existing directory) and the `--full-path` exemption both still apply to every pattern.\n- **New test in `tests/tests.rs`:** `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected` runs `fd foo --and one/two` and expects that error. It failed before the fix and fails again with `src/main.rs` reverted, so it really checks the fix.\n\n**Verified:**\n- `cargo test -q`: 139 unit tests and 111 integration tests pass.\n- `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` on `src` is clean.\n\n**Not run:**\n- `cargo fmt --check`, because rustfmt isn't installed here.\n- The Windows code path, since this machine is Linux.\n\n**Already broken:** `cargo clippy --all-targets` reports 14 \"redundant reference in `format!`\" errors in `tests/tests.rs`, for example at line 2529. They're in code I didn't change (it looks like a newer clippy lint), so I left them alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":403,"cache_read_input_tokens":41272,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":403,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4921241c-133a-4ac5-ad00-cbddd2996d55","uuid":"13cac7d0-5214-4fab-abf6-74f81f5c524a","timestamp":"2026-10-